{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Sign-In with Elevated Risk or New Behavior",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Initial Access / T1078\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Sign-In with Elevated Risk or New Behavior\" or \"<ip>|Okta Sign-In with Elevated Risk or New Behavior\"\n\nUses Okta's own risk engine on user.session.start. High (risk floor 75) when Okta rates the sign-in HIGH risk (securityContext.risk.level) or flags Velocity or New Country; Medium (floor 55) when Okta rates it MEDIUM. A new device, IP or location alone at LOW risk is not alerted because Okta already weighed it. Both successful and failed sign-ins are included. Replaces a rule that matched a display message Okta does not emit.\n\nFalse positives: travel, new devices, ISP changes. Tune with okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_new_authentication_behavior_detection/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_new_authentication_behavior_detection.toml",
  "GUID": "98f6ea5b-9268-58a6-8ffc-ea37a913ceb6",
